  "ingredients": [
    "2 teaspoons butter",
    "4 tablespoons all-purpose flour",
    "1.5 cups milk",
    "1 teaspoon salt",
    "0.25 teaspoon ground black pepper",
    "0.5 cup dry bread crumbs, browned in butter",
    "20 asparagus tips",
    "5 hard-boiled eggs, chopped"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "To make the white sauce: Melt butter in a small skillet over medium-low heat; stir in flour, then milk. Cook until thickened and season with salt and pepper.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "To make the casserole: Spread 1/2 of browned bread crumbs in the bottom of a 9x13-inch baking dish. Add layers of asparagus and chopped egg, alternately. Pour white sauce over all and top with remaining bread crumbs.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven for 30 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    }
